<http://data.silknow.org/object/b24c70f5-5460-3c99-9981-581302b6c5c5>
        a                       ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment            "Shawl of woven silk, England, ca. 1820-1840"@en , "Shawl of woven silk. With a repeating design of a thin-stemmed plant with flowers and curling tendrils within a border of large flowers and leaves. It is woven with a yellow silk warp and purple-blue silk weft in a 3/1 weft twill and its warp twill reverse, making the shawl reversible, and with a shot effect. The silk has a four cord selvedge woven in tabby and a short simple warp fringe."@en ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note        "Shawl of woven silk, England, ca. 1820-1840"@en , "Shawl of woven silk. With a repeating design of a thin-stemmed plant with flowers and curling tendrils within a border of large flowers and leaves. It is woven with a yellow silk warp and purple-blue silk weft in a 3/1 weft twill and its warp twill reverse, making the shawl reversible, and with a shot effect. The silk has a four cord selvedge woven in tabby and a short simple warp fringe."@en ;
